  "notes": "{自炊|じすい} means cooking for oneself at home, as opposed to eating out or buying ready-made food. Especially associated with students and people living alone.\n\nWRITING:\n{自|じ} (self) + {炊|すい} (cook rice). Literally \"cooking (rice) for oneself.\"\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {自炊|じすい}する: to cook for oneself\n- {自炊|じすい}{生活|せいかつ}: life of cooking for oneself\n- {自炊|じすい}を{始|はじ}める: to start cooking for oneself\n- {自炊|じすい}{派|は}: someone who prefers cooking at home\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {外食|がいしょく}: eating out at restaurants\n- コンビニ{弁当|べんとう}: convenience store bento\n- {中食|なかしょく}: buying prepared food to eat at home\n\nCULTURAL NOTE:\n{自炊|じすい} is a common topic when discussing {一人暮|ひとりぐ}らし (living alone). University students often start {自炊|じすい} for the first time when they move away from home.",
